---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import VarianceCalculator from "../../components/calculators/VarianceCalculator";

const seo = {
  page_description: "Calculate the variance and standard deviation of your daily metrics to understand your consistency.",
  open_graph_type: "website"
};
---
<Layout seo={seo} title="Variance Calculator | TrackAndLog">
  <main class="max-w-3xl mx-auto py-12 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="prose">
      <h1>Variance Calculator</h1>
      <p>While a rolling average shows your trend, variance shows your consistency. Are you hitting the same metric every day, or swinging wildly between extremes?</p>

      <noscript>
        <div class="bg-gray-100 p-4 border border-gray-300 my-4">
          <p><strong>JavaScript Required</strong></p>
          <p>This calculator requires JavaScript to run interactively. To calculate variance manually: find the mean, subtract the mean from each number and square the result, then find the average of those squared differences.</p>
        </div>
      </noscript>

      <VarianceCalculator client:load />

      <h2>Why calculate variance?</h2>
      <p>If you are tracking <a href="/metrics/sleep-duration">sleep duration</a>, averaging 7 hours might sound good. But if you get 4 hours one night and 10 the next, your high variance indicates poor sleep hygiene. Lowering your standard deviation is often just as important as raising your average.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
